{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"65ac97fd4eaec7a7","name":"card_unit_the_holy_boys","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_the_holy_boys","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"THE HOLY BOYS","text":"Once per turn, give your units +1+1 after you play a neutral card.","flavorText":"The Royal Norfolk Regiment inherited the nickname “The Holy Boys” from its predecessor, the 9th Regiment of Foot. During the Peninsular War, a Spanish soldier reportedly mistook the figure of Britannia on the regiment’s cap badge for the Virgin Mary, giving rise to this unusual nickname. The regiment received its “Royal” title in 1935 and went on to serve extensively during WWII. It fought in France in 1940, where the 2nd Battalion helped cover the retreat towards Dunkirk. In 1944, the 1st Battalion landed on Sword Beach on D-Day and fought through Normandy and the North West Europe campaign. Other battalions served in the Far East, notably at Singapore and in the Burma campaign. Five members of the regiment received the Victoria Cross during the war, reflecting the distinguished service of the “Holy Boys” across several theatres.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_the_holy_boys","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_the_holy_boys_title","SourceString":"THE HOLY BOYS","LocalizedString":"THE HOLY BOYS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_the_holy_boys_text","SourceString":"Once per turn, give your units +1+1 after you play a neutral card.","LocalizedString":"Once per turn, give your units +1+1 after you play a neutral card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_the_holy_boys_history","SourceString":"The Royal Norfolk Regiment inherited the nickname “The Holy Boys” from its predecessor, the 9th Regiment of Foot. During the Peninsular War, a Spanish soldier reportedly mistook the figure of Britannia on the regiment’s cap badge for the Virgin Mary, giving rise to this unusual nickname. The regiment received its “Royal” title in 1935 and went on to serve extensively during WWII. It fought in France in 1940, where the 2nd Battalion helped cover the retreat towards Dunkirk. In 1944, the 1st Battalion landed on Sword Beach on D-Day and fought through Normandy and the North West Europe campaign. Other battalions served in the Far East, notably at Singapore and in the Burma campaign. Five members of the regiment received the Victoria Cross during the war, reflecting the distinguished service of the “Holy Boys” across several theatres.","LocalizedString":"The Royal Norfolk Regiment inherited the nickname “The Holy Boys” from its predecessor, the 9th Regiment of Foot. During the Peninsular War, a Spanish soldier reportedly mistook the figure of Britannia on the regiment’s cap badge for the Virgin Mary, giving rise to this unusual nickname. The regiment received its “Royal” title in 1935 and went on to serve extensively during WWII. It fought in France in 1940, where the 2nd Battalion helped cover the retreat towards Dunkirk. In 1944, the 1st Battalion landed on Sword Beach on D-Day and fought through Normandy and the North West Europe campaign. Other battalions served in the Far East, notably at Singapore and in the Burma campaign. Five members of the regiment received the Victoria Cross during the war, reflecting the distinguished service of the “Holy Boys” across several theatres."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"hasGuard":true,"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/THE_HOLY_BOYS.THE_HOLY_B